data ci_v1_compiler_tests_compile_gate_eagain_retry_note: String = "ci_v1_compiler_tests_compile_gate_run_script routes through the same v2.workflow.ci_retry_emit ci_cargo_eagain_retry_script seam as ci_release_build_script (EAGAIN-detect → CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1 cold retry, keeps sscache, no RUSTC_WRAPPER drop). This is NOT a new fallback class: it widens the srvN open-thread population that docs/plans/srvn-buildcache-provisioning-design.md STEP 2 names for removal (operator-sequenced after T4 live read-back) — the same interim debt as the release build, not an independent mask. STEP 2 roll-up must retire level-1 retry on BOTH build-job consumers (ci_release_build_script and this run_script); this PR adds the second gate to that tracked population. Dissolves with ci_release_build_script when STEP 2 retires the level-1 arm or converts it to typed refusal. MEASURED EFFICACY, 2026-08-07: the level-1 arm does NOT recover the daemon-side failure. It keeps sccache and varies only CARGO_BUILD_JOBS, so when the failing resource is the sccache SERVER (failed to spawn, EAGAIN off the server socket) it addresses the wrong variable. Three PRs hit this on two srv1 slots in one day — 7983 on srv1-05 and 7974 on srv1-01 both failed THROUGH this retry and both passed on a plain re-run with zero code change — so each occurrence burns a second full cold build to fail again. The expected repair is therefore to drop RUSTC_WRAPPER on the retry and emit the CiSccacheProviderReceipt SKIPPED counted-degradation receipt this same file already models at provider-bind time, naming EAGAIN as the cause; that keeps the degradation typed and counted rather than silent, and is the arm already sanctioned here rather than a new escape hatch. w_gate_script_eagain_cold_retry previously asserted !without RUSTC_WRAPPER and !env -u RUSTC_WRAPPER, which made that repair fail a green test — DESIGN section 5's enshrined-degradation shape, where tests assert the fallback string and freeze it as the contract. Those two negative assertions are removed so STEP 2 is a code change rather than a test deletion; the retry itself is unchanged and remains tracked debt."

fn ci_v1_compiler_tests_compile_gate_run_script() -> String {
  let _note = ci_v1_compiler_tests_compile_gate_eagain_retry_note
  concat(
    "set -e\n",
    concat(
      concat("ROOT=", ci_repo_root_shell(), "\n"),
      concat(
        concat(
          "# ",
          concat(dissolution_description(condition: ci_v1_compiler_tests_compile_gate_shell_emit_dissolution_trigger), "\n")
        ),
        ci_cargo_eagain_retry_script(command: ci_v1_compiler_tests_compile_gate_command())
      )
    )
  )
}

