data gunbc_ci_workflow_wrapper_timeout_minutes: Duration = minute_count(m: gunbc_ci_workflow_wrapper_budget_minutes())

data gunbc_ci_regen_step_timeout_minutes: Duration = 15

data gunbc_ci_regen_step_timeout_note: String = "The regen step gets its OWN budget (operator main-timeout ruling 2026-07-23): it measured ~5min on every recent green run, and it previously borrowed the floor step's cap — which double-counted the floor budget in the job backstop sum and let a wedged regen sit for hours. 15m = 3x the measured envelope; a regen that exceeds it is a defect to diagnose, never headroom to grant."

data gunbc_ci_floor_step_timeout_discovery_flip_note: String = "COST WALL landed 2026-07-23 (CI floor endgame, appended per the raise-discipline this history IS the receipt for): the bounce pattern below — every raise fitting the cap to the cost — now has its construction answer: per-BATCH clamps derived from data (gunbc.ci_spec gunbc_ci_floor_batch_clamp_params, superseding the 53m static gunbc_ci_floor_batch_wall_budget_seconds list) enforced by claim_executor as typed FLOOR-BATCH-OVER-BUDGET refusals with per-batch receipt rows, so a lane that adds minutes reds ITS batch at merge time instead of bouncing this cap upward later. This cap is unchanged by that PR; 55 -> 40 is proposed as a data change AFTER the post-merge receipts exist (operator signs). PRIOR HISTORY: -> 55 operator ruling 2026-07-23 (main wall ~75m: 'even 1 hour is absolutely ridiculous'): the 270 cap legalized a 4.5-hour crawl — receipt run 29976854620 @ 76fa6548e killed by hand at t=227m with current=16.3G pinned at memory.high, swap=34.4G, high_events=37,096,823, psi_some_avg10=33.82, oom_kill=0, governor 'hard back-off 1->1' every few seconds: the memory.high throttle-crawl class (retention finally exceeded the slot cap; the prior 40-50m greens were already pinned at 15.2-16.1G with zero headroom), and 8 subsequent main pushes wedged identically behind it fleet-wide. Recent green floors run 39-45m, so 55 is a real ceiling not a target; the regression ledger to hold onto: ~8m pre-#6848 -> ~18m (#6848) -> 40-50m (retention accreting to the cap) -> 4h (cap lost) — one disease (retention, not footprint), never an accepted baseline. Named follow-ups so this cap becomes the backstop rather than the diagnostic: the governor gains a terminal crawl-refusal arm (sustained high_events storm at width=1 -> typed FloorRefusedMemoryBudget naming batch/peak/swap, minutes not hours), and the #7106-attributed levers (one-tree-one-resolve, #6848 once-per-entry fixpoint, M2 eviction) bring the floor back under the cap with margin. Superseded main runs are NOT cancelled by policy (operator 2026-07-23): the per-commit verdict history is bisection evidence — the timeout IS the bound. PRIOR HISTORY: -> 270 restored 2026-07-12 on #6512 after 60m fail-fast regressed merge CI (receipt run 29197126623 @ 35f212fa5d: 60m step kill with 0 witness FAILs — batch-1 compile-clean PASS @ 15:01, batch-2 skip walk ~26m to recompute_trace_probe_test, then ~34m silent eval until kill; same serial-floor-wall class as 29183446733). Prior -> 60 operator ruling 2026-07-12: lower floor step cap from 270m so CI fails fast while the serial floor wall is debugged separately (receipt run 29183446733 @ 2e856a5617: 270m kill with 0 witness FAILs, batch-2 still in discovery SKIP walk). Prior -> 270 at PR #6464 receipt run 29151777611 (2026-07-11): 180m step cap still timed out mid batch 2 — 1535 SKIP rows finished @ 12:35:43, then ~147m silent witness-execution phase until the 180m kill @ 15:03:12 with batch 2 never completing (~177m in-batch from 12:06:38; ~443 non-skipped rows in roster of 1978). Prior -> 180 at run 29148344466 (~116m in-batch, ~87m post-skip). Prior -> 120 at run 29145270700. Prior -> 90 at run 29141663541. Prior -> 90 at body_lowering normalize hook (#6459 receipt run 29148735992 @ 3a372b7: floor step timed out at 60m MID discovery corpus after ~320 SKIP lines — batch-1 compile-clean normalize reconcile ~263s with body_lowering_fold in the normalize import closure; discovery still resolves every unique entry file before skip, so resolve->normalize pulled the ~1.3k-line scaffold into most closure walks). Structural fix on the same lane: NormalizedTree moved to v2.compiler.normalized_tree so v2.compiler.resolve no longer imports normalize (dissolve-on: skip-before-resolve so skipped rows never pay entry resolve). Prior step budget -> 60 at the discovery flip (gunbc.ci_spec ci_spec_discovery_flip_note; authored as 30 -> 60 on #6403, main had meanwhile bumped 30 -> 45 with the #6422 enrollments): the corpus discovery batch adds a whole-tree resolve plus the always-run live-tree rows to the floor step. Discovery corpus spawn_width_cap stays pinned to 1 (ci_corpus_discovery_spawn_width_cap in v2.workflow.ci_floor_plan): at width W the executor holds the parent's process-shared index PLUS W private shard indexes ((1+W) x whole-tree residency; width=2 OOM receipt run 28999086030), while width=1 runs rows on the main thread against the ONE shared index (union-resolve S1). CORRECTED RECEIPT (2026-07-10): run 29000557166's floor did NOT complete - the executor was host-OOM-killed ~8min in, MID discovery corpus (the log's later ExitSuccess belongs to the merge-admission STAMP tool, which stamped CI_FLOOR_EXIT=137); no flipped corpus has completed in CI yet - the only completion receipt is local (33.5GiB container, ~40min at width 5). The kill vector is host-level oversubscription (see gunbc_falsifier_plan_spawn_width_note), not this width model. #6475 receipt run 29143617420 @ 0c0f73: batch-1 compile-clean ~4m green; batch-2 discovery killed at 90m step cap mid-manual (last skip rust_wire_serde @ 07:47:49; ~15GiB peak). #6475 receipt run 29146814967 @ 6a61fce: same stall at 120m (last skip rust_wire_serde @ 09:34:49; ~85m silent eval). #6475 receipt run 29150477894 @ 6cd5326: same stall at 180m (last skip rust_wire_serde @ 11:43:46; ~88m silent eval) — local gunbc run on s1_closure_parses_holds reads 3/40 closure paths in 10m before timeout, matching the silent-eval class (live filesystem_read per path, not a skip-logged row). #6475 receipt run 29161709373 @ 9d9852c: batch-1 compile-clean refused — gunbc_ci_floor_step_timeout_discovery_flip_note string literal terminated early at col 2043 (body_lowering suffix spliced after closing quote during rebase merge); restored single-line literal on rebase to main #6464 note. Revisit down when floor memoization / resolver graph-major shrink the resolve wall; the affected-set selection receipts (skip counts per PR) are the cost dial to watch."

data gunbc_ci_step_timeout_measure_grounding_disposition: Disposition = Scaffold {
  dissolves_to: SingleAuthority,
  bind: DeclarationRef {
    module_path: "gunbc.ci_workflow",
    decl_name: "gunbc_ci_workflow_wrapper_timeout_minutes",
    field: WholeDeclaration
  }
}

data gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes: Int = 5

data gunbc_ci_v1_compiler_tests_compile_gate_timeout_minutes: Duration = 15

data gunbc_ci_v1_compiler_tests_compile_gate_timeout_note: String = "v1-compiler-tests retained-kernel execution gate step budget. Originally a compile-contract gate (operator ruling 2026-08-05, PR A / fierce-heron-177): reordered after the release build and switched to cargo test --release --no-run so v1-compiler compiles once per job. --no-run removed 2026-08-11 with the suite cutover; the crate shrank from 98 modules / 740 tests to the 9 declared retained modules / 30 tests, which execute rather than only compile. Warm runs should complete in seconds once the release artifact is warm; 15m retains the prior cold-host envelope without raising the cap."

data gunbc_ci_stage0_partition_compile_gate_timeout_minutes: Int = 15

data gunbc_ci_stage0_partition_compile_gate_timeout_note: String = "stage0 partition compile gate step budget (sharp-fox-403 C1): seven sequential cargo check -p v1-stage0-* partition crates enrolled as the build-job compile backstop over stage0_partition_crate_rows. Cold-host envelope matches v1-compiler-tests compile gate until a dedicated receipt exists; warm partition crates are smaller than the monolith test crate."

data gunbc_ci_v1_compiler_test_targets_compile_gate_timeout_minutes: Int = 10

data gunbc_ci_v1_compiler_test_targets_compile_gate_timeout_note: String = "v1-compiler test-targets compile gate step budget. 10 minutes against 67s MEASURED for this step's exact argv (cargo check -p v1-compiler --all-targets, cold, remote runner, on the repaired tree after gunbc#8167 / gunbc#8173 landed the lib-test compile fix). The earlier figure recorded here was 99s from cargo check --workspace --all-targets, which was an upper BOUND rather than this step's cost — it was all that could be measured while main's lib test target did not compile, and it is superseded rather than kept beside the real number. Deliberately BELOW the 15m carried by the v1-compiler-tests and partition gates rather than copied from them: those two inherited a cold-host envelope with no dedicated receipt, and repeating a number nobody measured is how an unmeasured envelope becomes precedent. The gate runs AFTER the release build for the same reason the retained-kernel gate does — v1-compiler is already compiled in release with the shared feature set, so the check reuses that artifact instead of forcing a second compile. Raising this needs a measurement, not a round number."

data gunbc_ci_artifact_transfer_step_timeout_minutes: Int = 10

data gunbc_ci_artifact_transfer_step_note: String = "Cross-job handoff of the release bins (operator job-split ruling 2026-07-11): the build job packs ci_floor_required_artifact_names into one tgz (tar preserves the executable bits a raw artifact zip would drop) and uploads it; the ci floor job downloads, unpacks into target/release, and re-verifies via claim_executor --verify-build-artifacts before any step consumes a bin (fail-closed: a missing or truncated artifact reds the job at the verify, never as a mid-floor bin fallback). 10m is the transfer envelope for a ~200MB archive under fleet pressure; upload uses if-no-files-found: error so an empty pack is loud."

data gunbc_ci_selection_control_step_timeout_minutes: Int = 15

data gunbc_ci_selection_control_step_note: String = "The affected-set selection control suite as a per-PR gate (operator fork (c), 2026-07-10 — the acceptance's 'green AND wired' half): floor_skip_discovery_witness runs the hermetic skip/refuse/divergence controls, including predict_only_red_predicted_unaffected_is_divergence — the discriminating RED for the falsifier's divergence counting — and the empty-diff-skips pin (ruling 2026-07-05: a failure arm refuses, never widens). DEMOTED to the falsifier cadence 2026-07-29 (operator ruling, PR-timing analysis) — it no longer rides the per-PR ci job; the coverage delta and detection window are stated at the end of this note. Hermetic: both diff channels are injected (floor_diff_observe.dag's floor_observe_git_diff_unified/floor_observe_git_diff_name_status GUNBC_CI_DIFF_UNIFIED/GUNBC_CI_DIFF_NAME_STATUS arms), so the suite measures fixtures, never this checkout's real diff. Budget: 80s measured local (2026-07-10, full suite, release build); 15m is the fleet-pressure envelope, a named term in the ci backstop sum. MEASURED CORRECTION 2026-07-29: the 80s local basis above had drifted 6.8x — the step measured 9m02s on the fleet (run 30482171871, job 90679506428, 19:22:04 to 19:31:06), about 27 percent of a 33.6-minute ci job wall, and nothing alarmed because the 15m step cap left it at 60 percent of its ceiling. The step's own in-code note (floor_skip_discovery_witness.rs) had already recorded a 4m51s-vs-80s incident and the D3 fix for it, so this is that same class regressed to ~1.9x the state the fix was written to repair. ACCOUNTING, from the job log: the assertions cost nothing (every witness row reports 0.0-0.3ms); the wall is 18 serial scenario setups — ~4m49s for two whole-corpus index builds (one shared-index build plus budget_roster_resolves_cold, the deliberate Class-B pool-coincidence control), ~34s for the eight scenarios that hit the shared index and report 'unaffected (import-closure, skipped without resolve)', ~3m30s for the ~7 scenarios that land 'in the affected closure (resolving to decide node-frontier)' at ~30s per resolve, and 11.2s of thread-local teardown. RESPONSE, in the order the costs were priced: (a) the step is now affected-set scoped by ci_selection_control_skip_step (v2.workflow.ci_workflow_run_emit ci_selection_control_skip_policy_note) — the mechanism applied to itself, pull_request-gated with push-to-main as the unconditional cold control. That is the lever that matters, but it is a TRADE, not a free win, and the numbers are in that policy note: the skip witness costs ~100s per invocation (the cold whole-pool index its diff observation builds), so a skipping PR saves ~7m22s while a non-skipping PR pays ~100s MORE than before. MEASURED SKIP RATE 23 of the last 100 main commits (35 touch src/v1/**, 36 touch markdown, 1 touches Cargo config, and 13 of the remainder intersect the suite's actual 391-file dag closure), for an expected ~-25s/PR — about 1.2 percent of the job. That supersedes two earlier claims in the policy note, -7.7 min/PR (unmeasured 85 percent) and -4.3 min/PR (a <=66 percent ceiling extrapolated from the src/v1/** prefix before markdown and the closure were counted); both are kept visible there rather than replaced. So the cost win alone does not carry the scaffold under DESIGN §6 — the ~100s cold diff observation is what ruins the mean, and it is an already-named deficit this change did not create. (b) the teardown path is removed BY CONSTRUCTION — the suite now exits via process::exit, which does not run thread-local destructors, so cli_run's whole-pool Rc index is never dropped. HONESTY ON THIS ONE: the 11.2s is the CI-MEASURED cost of the path that was removed (the unlogged gap between the final receipt line and step completion on run 30482171871), and the removal is a property of process::exit rather than an inference; what was NOT done is an end-to-end before/after local re-measure, because the suite exceeds the local measurement window available here. So read (b) as mechanism-plus-prior-measurement, not as a fresh paired timing — the next CI run of the unscoped arm is where the paired number lands. STILL OWED, deliberately not fixed here: the ~30s-per-node-frontier-resolve unit is unexplained — it is 4x the ~7.2s/resolve the floor resolve receipt records, so it is either a genuinely larger closure or a PROCESS_RESOLVE_STORE miss, and it wants a measurement rather than a guess. PLACEMENT CALL MADE (operator ruling 2026-07-29, PR-timing analysis) — this note's own line above held the falsifier-cadence question 'for an operator call because that is the placement decision the D3b gate flip mispriced'. The call is: the WHOLE step rides gunbc.falsifier_workflow, not just budget_roster_resolves_cold. IT SUBSUMES THE (a) TRADE RATHER THAN COMPETING WITH IT, using this note's own measured numbers: (a) left a skipping PR paying ~100s and a NON-skipping PR paying 542s + ~100s, at a measured 23-of-100 skip rate for an expected ~-25s/PR, which is why this note already concluded the cost win alone does not carry the scaffold under DESIGN §6. Demotion moves the step and its in-script skip together, so the per-PR job loses BOTH the 542s suite and the ~100s cold diff observation — about -642s on the 77 percent that do not skip and -100s on the rest, dominating the trade instead of tuning it. The ~100s double payment the yellow dissolve-on below counts is halved in the same motion, since only regen_floor_skip_witness still pays it per PR. THE SKIP STAYS CORRECT UNDER DEMOTION BY CONSTRUCTION: ci_selection_control_skip_step's condition is StrEq on \"$GITHUB_EVENT_NAME\" == pull_request, so on the falsifier's schedule event it cannot fire and the suite runs UNCONDITIONALLY — which is exactly the cold-control posture, the same shape as the two controls it now sits beside. MEASUREMENT BASIS, dated honestly: the demotion was priced at 10m09s median on the per-PR ci job (n=6 green runs, range 8m41s-10m32s), which is a WIDER sample than the single 9m02s run above but was taken BEFORE (a) and (b) landed, so it does not credit the teardown removal or the skip. The post-(a)/(b) per-PR number is therefore OWED and not claimed here; the demotion does not rest on it, because (a)'s own measured expectation is only ~-25s/PR and the non-skipping majority still pays minutes. PLACEMENT on the falsifier is load-bearing twice and pinned structurally (test.claim.falsifier_workflow_witness_test): AFTER the release build, because the step executes the release-built floor_skip_discovery_witness, and BEFORE ci_floor_peak_pre_step, because that pair brackets the floor's cgroup measurement and a step inside it would attribute its own residency to the floor's peak receipt. Exactly-one on the falsifier, zero on ci, asserted in both directions — a yaml substring presence test passes for every permutation and cannot express either invariant. COVERAGE DELTA, and the earlier claim retracted: a PR that reintroduces a widen now reds when the NEXT COMPLETED falsifier control runs, NOT 'within one 4h cadence window' (review correction 2026-07-30 — that claim was too strong). The falsifier is queue-not-cancel with a 230-minute backstop class and this step sits after the prelude and release build, so a change landing just after a run passed the control waits for that run's remainder, plus queued-run startup, plus the next run's prelude and build — a sum that can exceed one cadence period. What bounds the damage is unchanged: a widen is bounded by the status quo (per-PR the witness would not have run at all), and the divergence is COUNTED when detected, never absorbed. RETURN TRIGGER, stated as an OUTCOME rather than a mechanism (review correction 2026-07-30 — the prior text prescribed per-gate pooled children, a fix that had already landed while the suite still measured minutes, so it named a stale mechanism as its own re-entry condition): re-enrol per-PR once a named receipt shows the ENTIRE step, spawn to verdict, on the CI fleet rather than a local host, consistently below a seconds-scale ceiling across a full falsifier window. Whichever mechanism buys that — the persistent content-keyed node store the yellow dissolve-on names, witness realization to native bins, or something else — is the lane's business, not this note's. BUDGET: the 15m envelope is retained as a named term in the FALSIFIER backstop sum; the ci backstop drops the same term and falls 115m -> 100m, which is why the two edits are one change and not two."

data gunbc_ci_prelude_allowance_minutes: Int = 5

data gunbc_ci_release_build_step_timeout_minutes: Int = 45

data srv1_dashboard_deploy_concurrency_group: String = "srv1-dashboard-deploy"
data srv1_dashboard_deploy_serialization_note: String = "Blue/green selection is observe-then-mutate, so two deploy jobs may not overlap: both could observe blue active, then the first flips green while the second restarts what has become the active green slot, recreating the outage. Job-grain concurrency serializes the entire cutover with cancel-in-progress=false; QueueNotMax may replace an older pending deployment with the newest main revision, but it never interrupts the one holding the host mutation window."

fn gunbc_ci_build_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() -> Int {
  gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_v1_compiler_tests_compile_gate_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_stage0_partition_compile_gate_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_v1_compiler_test_targets_compile_gate_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_release_build_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_artifact_transfer_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_prelude_allowance_minutes
}

data gunbc_ci_receipt_gate_steps_moved_in_executor_note: String = "The resolve-receipt and materialization-receipt gate STEPS are deleted (ruling 2026-07-30): their laws — resolves_total equals the declared count, and the materialization receipt exists/parses/keyed nonzero — now run INSIDE claim_executor as ordinary-floor finalization (run_walk, FloorFinalization), so a receipt-law violation blocks every on-success stage instead of redding a step AFTER admission had already stamped. The two aux terms leave the backstop sum in the same motion, keeping it the exact step-sum + prelude the witness pins. The receipt FILES keep writing — they are observability the falsifier and operators read — only the shell re-validation of them is gone, because keeping it would be a second representation of the floor-completion rule."

fn gunbc_ci_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() -> Int {
  gunbc_ci_artifact_transfer_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_workflow_wrapper_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_prelude_allowance_minutes
}

fn gunbc_ci_regen_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() -> Int {
  gunbc_ci_artifact_transfer_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_regen_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_prelude_allowance_minutes
}

data gunbc_ci_job_backstop_timeout_disposition: Disposition = Terminal {
  reason: "gunbc CI budget semantics (operator ruling 2026-07-06): floor step gunbc_ci_floor_step_timeout_minutes enforced at STEP level (RED-by-failure); ci job backstop gunbc_ci_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() = release build + floor + aux + prelude (100m at floor=45m after #6422 witness-cone receipt; was 85m at floor=30m after #6361 Lever A dissolve-on; was 65m at floor=10m) so cold release build is not killed by a job cap shorter than gunbc_ci_release_build_step_timeout_minutes (receipt run 28819559597 @ 201371c: 10m job kill aborted cargo mid-build). The accumulator-copy roster gate is OFFLINE, not CI-enrolled (operator ruling 2026-07-10): its three witness entries re-parse rostered files under the interpreter (~15m serial measured; receipt: run 29066265723 hit the then-30m step cap with the gate enrolled on a 27m40s baseline floor) — re-enroll when parse/resolve memoization or batch-1 shared-parse reuse shrinks the gate to seconds. The job cap must cover step budgets so gates reach RED-by-step-failure, not job-cancelled silent-pass (#6323 starvation-kill scoped to ci/floor only on main; the rust_tests job and its warm/gate step-sum backstop were removed 2026-07-11 to free runner capacity). dissolve-on: compile-clean scoping/memoization shrinks batch-1; floor step raised when batch-1 completes inside measured envelope (receipt run 28902523405 @ e1a27e4286). #6422 receipt run 29065683045 @ a2bcd6f668: batches 1-3 ~20m (dag_collect_fingerprint_witness_keystone_holds 488s), batch 4 rust_monolith_gate still running at 30m step kill — raised floor to 45m (= rust gate step budget). 2026-07-10 step-budget completeness (review catch, #6438): the resolve-receipt gate step had NO step cap — a hang there could only die by job-cancel, the same starvation-kill class — so it now carries the aux cap (the script is a sub-second receipt read) and the ci backstop counts the aux steps exactly. Every ci-job step now has a declared step budget and the backstop is the exact step-sum + prelude. 2026-07-10 merge of #6441 into #6438: the incoming materialization receipt gate step landed uncapped (timeout none) — same class — so the merge resolution capped it aux too; the ci backstop counts FIVE aux terms: peak pre-read, peak post-read, resolve-receipt gate, materialization receipt gate, merge-admission gate. 2026-07-10 selection-control wiring (operator fork (c)): the affected-set selection control step (floor_skip_discovery_witness, see gunbc_ci_selection_control_step_note) joins the ci job with its OWN named budget gunbc_ci_selection_control_step_timeout_minutes (15m; 80s measured local) — a named term in the backstop sum, not a sixth aux term — so the backstop stays the exact step-sum + prelude. 2026-07-11 serial job split (operator ruling): the single ci job became three serially-chained jobs — build (release build + pack/upload of the ci_floor_required_artifact_names manifest; backstop gunbc_ci_build_job_backstop_timeout_minutes()), ci (downloads + verifies the release-bins artifact, then regen/floor/receipts/selection/admission; backstop gunbc_ci_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() with the release-build term replaced by artifact-transfer + unpack terms), and emit_determinism (needs ci; the x2 full-corpus emit oracle extracted from the floor batches via the GithubActionsEmitDeterminismJob surface; backstop gunbc_ci_emit_determinism_job_backstop_timeout_minutes()). Rationale: a cold monolith build (~33-34min measured, runs 29125380927/29126347183 — sccache healthy at 96% Rust hits, zero read errors; the wall is one true-miss compile of the 161k-line v1-compiler crate, and per-host sccache caches mean a cross-host repeat pays it again) consumed the shared job budget so every .rs-touching merge ran at the ceiling by construction; each unit now carries its own bounded, monitored budget and a timeout is attributable at job grain. The chain is strictly serial (build -> ci -> emit_determinism), so the concurrent runner-slot footprint stays one job per run. Honesty row: emit_determinism lands NON-required on the gunbc main ruleset (the same status ci_regen had before #6470 folded it in; only the ci job is protection-required) — the oracle still runs and reds loudly every merge, but enforcing it is an operator ruleset action; its per-merge-required return trigger is that ruleset flip, and its deeper dissolve-on is the §7 self-host frontier retiring the v1 seed emitter whose host-Rust nondeterminism class it guards. SUPERSEDED 2026-07-14 (this PR, Phase D): the emit_determinism job, its x2 sampling oracle (tools.emit_determinism_gate/_transport, both deleted), and the GithubActionsEmitDeterminismJob surface were REMOVED — so ci_build_job -> ci_job is now the whole serial chain and this note's emit_determinism terms are historical. Determinism became a construction gate (§5 construction-over-validation): v2.lens.determinism.determinism_compile_gate enrolled in v2.compiler.compile always_required_root_lenses (mirrors accumulator_copy #6527) reds any bare map_keys reach into the v2 compile door, and C.2 (#6576) made the v1 seed emitter map_keys-free by construction so its host-Rust class needs no x2 sample. Operator ruling 2026-07-14 (b): the dying §7 seed carries no active guard; the construction guarantee replaces the sampling oracle. Class-4 correction (operator 2026-07-26): the deleted orphan gunbc_ci_job_timeout_policy_minutes (90, zero consumers) is NOT this authority — the live ci job reads gunbc_ci_job_backstop_timeout_minutes(), which is the composed step-sum + prelude (witness: ci_job_backstop_is_step_sum_plus_prelude)."
}

data gunbc_ci_job_timeout_policy_minutes_deleted_note: String = "Deleted class-4 orphan (operator ruling 2026-07-26): gunbc_ci_job_timeout_policy_minutes (=90) had zero corpus consumers; the live ci job timeout is gunbc_ci_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() (composed step-sum + prelude). Inventory row corrected to name the backstop fn, not the dead literal."

// ── Unified fleet job (operator request 2026-08-10: "a single fleet convergence job —
// it's overwhelming to see so many"). The ten former deploy/convergence/toolbox jobs
// collapse into ONE `fleet` job so the GHA UI shows a single row instead of ~nine
// (mostly-skipped) ones. Each step keeps the event guard its former job's if_condition
// carried, applied per-step via with_step_if; the shared prelude + release-bins + WIF/
// agent setup run ONCE, and the key-agent cleanup runs always(). The step builders the
// former jobs used are all retained and reused below — only the per-op JOB wrappers are
// removed. ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// Overwrite a step's if_condition (steps arrive from the builders with if_condition:none;
// the coproduct must be rebuilt to set the field).
fn with_step_if(step: Step, cond: String) -> Step {
  match step {
    RunStep { name: n, id: i, run: r, shell: sh, env: e, working_directory: wd, if_condition: _, continue_on_error: coe, timeout_minutes: tm } =>
      RunStep { name: n, id: i, run: r, shell: sh, env: e, working_directory: wd, if_condition: Present { value: cond }, continue_on_error: coe, timeout_minutes: tm }
    UsesStep { name: n, id: i, uses: u, with: w, env: e, if_condition: _, continue_on_error: coe, timeout_minutes: tm } =>
      UsesStep { name: n, id: i, uses: u, with: w, env: e, if_condition: Present { value: cond }, continue_on_error: coe, timeout_minutes: tm }
  }
}

// OBSERVATION UNFUSED FROM ACTUATION (operator route 2026-08-10, CONVERGE acceptance).
// deploy dashboard and advance refs/fleet/desired are WRITES — they stay push-only, so the
// job-if's !cancelled() + main + needs.ci.result == 'success' guard is what gates them, and
// a censored/red floor can never let them run. collect_fleet_convergence is a READ: it
// collects host receipts and folds a verdict, and reading what the hosts CURRENTLY report
// does not require THIS commit's floor to be green. So the collector also runs on
// workflow_dispatch. This is NOT a weakening of the gate — it separates observing fleet
// state from changing it; a dispatch-collected fold describes state relative to the CURRENT
// refs/fleet/desired (not the dispatched head), so it never advances anything and never
// stands in for a green-floor acceptance. It exists because two consecutive main pushes hit
// the cold whole-corpus floor over-budget, so the push-gated collector never got to run and
// items 3 (per-host receipts) and 5 (the fold) had zero executions.
data ci_fleet_convergence_write_if: String = "github.event_name == 'push'"
data ci_fleet_collect_read_if: String = "github.event_name == 'push' || github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch'"

// Main-push convergence steps: deploy stage(s) + collect + advance. Deploy and advance are
// push-only WRITES; collect is a READ admitted on push OR workflow_dispatch (see above).
fn ci_fleet_convergence_steps() -> List<Step> {
  concat(
    map(gunbc_ci_deploy_stages, s => with_step_if(step: ci_deploy_step(stage: s), cond: ci_fleet_convergence_write_if)),
    [
      with_step_if(step: ci_collect_fleet_convergence_step(), cond: ci_fleet_collect_read_if),
      with_step_if(step: ci_advance_fleet_desired_step(), cond: ci_fleet_convergence_write_if)
    ]
  )
}

// workflow_dispatch toolbox steps: scan -> enroll -> probe (+multi-principal) ->
// observe_probe -> timer -> authorized-key -> observe_tasks, each guarded to dispatch.
// Serialized (former parallel jobs), which is if anything MORE correct — enroll after
// scan, probe after enroll.
fn ci_fleet_dispatch_steps() -> List<Step> {
  map(
    [
      ci_fleet_host_key_scan_step(),
      ci_fleet_host_key_enroll_step(),
      ci_fleet_reach_probe_step(),
      ci_multi_principal_probe_step(),
      ci_probe_identity_observe_step(),
      ci_authorized_key_enroll_step(),
      ci_srv1_tasks_observation_step()
    ],
    st => with_step_if(step: st, cond: "github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch'")
  )
}

// Fleet job backstop = prelude allowance + all aux steps in the LARGER (dispatch) branch.
// Shared aux: release-download, unpack-verify, WIF, key-agent, cleanup (5). Dispatch ops:
// 8. Only one branch runs per event, so the dispatch branch (13 aux) dominates the push
// branch (5 shared + 3 ops = 8). Cap, not expected runtime — each aux step self-caps.
fn gunbc_ci_fleet_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() -> Int {
  gunbc_ci_prelude_allowance_minutes + (13 * gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes)
}

// Union of the former jobs' grants: WIF / deploy / collect need id_token:write; advance
// needs contents:write.
fn ci_fleet_permissions() -> WorkflowPermissions {
  WorkflowPermissions {
    contents: Present { value: extdeps.github.actions.PermWrite },
    pull_requests: none,
    issues: none,
    actions: none,
    id_token: Present { value: extdeps.github.actions.PermWrite }
  }
}

fn ci_fleet_job() -> Job {
  Job {
    id: "fleet",
    name: none,
    runner: gunbc_ci_deploy_srv1_runner_spec(),
    steps: concat(
      concat(
        ci_artifact_consumer_prelude_steps(),
        [ci_release_bins_download_step(), ci_release_bins_unpack_verify_step(), ci_fleet_wif_auth_step(), ci_fleet_key_agent_step()]
      ),
      concat(
        ci_fleet_convergence_steps(),
        concat(ci_fleet_dispatch_steps(), [ci_fleet_key_agent_cleanup_step()])
      )
    ),
    needs: ["ci"],
    env: none,
    outputs: none,
    if_condition: Present { value: ci_fleet_job_if },
    timeout_minutes: Present { value: gunbc_ci_fleet_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() },
    continue_on_error: none,
    concurrency: Present {
      value: ConcurrencyMappingQueueNotMax {
        group: srv1_dashboard_deploy_concurrency_group,
        cancel_in_progress: Present { value: CancelInProgressBool { value: false } },
        explicit_single: none,
      }
    },
    permissions: Present { value: ci_fleet_permissions() }
  }
}

// Read-only srv1 tasks pre-apply observation (operator ruling 2026-08-09 on PR 8045,
// manager approval msg_03ec1f78): workflow_dispatch-ONLY at the job condition, so it
// never rides pull_request or push events; pinned to the srv1 runner so the read runs
// INSIDE the observed universe; needs only the release-bins build (no floor, no deploy
// chain). The step is strictly read-only — the entry it invokes reaches only systemctl
// show and cgroupfs filesystem_read (gunbc.srv1_tasks_preapply_observation), and the
// printed return value is the typed Srv1TasksPreApplyReceipt.
fn ci_srv1_tasks_observation_step() -> Step {
  RunStep {
    name: Present { value: "Read-only srv1 tasks pre-apply observation (observe_srv1_tasks_preapply_wet)" },
    id: none,
    run: gunbc_ci_srv1_tasks_observation_invoke(),
    shell: none,
    env: none,
    working_directory: none,
    if_condition: none,
    continue_on_error: none,
    timeout_minutes: Present { value: gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes }
  }
}

// Main→desired-ref advancement job (CONVERGE-0 loop): push-to-main only, downstream of
// the required ci check (needs: [ci] is the floor-green admission), contents:write so the
// checkout-persisted credential can push the CAS ref advance. No host is contacted; hosts
// follow the ref on their own timers.
// Live fleet reach probe (loop leg e): workflow_dispatch-only, srv1-pinned (the probe
// runs FROM inside the fleet, over the typed SSH probe seam where outcome is data).
fn ci_multi_principal_probe_step() -> Step {
  RunStep {
    name: Present { value: "Read-only multi-principal fleet-key probe on srv3/srv4 (fleet_multi_principal_probe_wet; hostname + sudo -n -l; no writes)" },
    id: none,
    run: gunbc_ci_multi_principal_probe_invoke(),
    shell: none,
    env: none,
    working_directory: none,
    if_condition: none,
    continue_on_error: none,
    timeout_minutes: Present { value: gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes }
  }
}

fn ci_fleet_reach_probe_step() -> Step {
  RunStep {
    name: Present { value: "Live fleet reach probe (probe_fleet_reach_wet; outcomes are data)" },
    id: none,
    run: gunbc_ci_fleet_reach_probe_invoke(),
    shell: none,
    env: none,
