data ci_regen_job_note: String = "The self-host fixed-point regen as its OWN job upstream of ci (operator-directed 2026-07-23: 'regen should be upstream of ci — doesn't ci depend on regen passing anyway?'). It was a step inside the ci job (folded in #6470, 2026-07-11); extracting it makes the dependency explicit — ci needs [build, regen], so a regen fixed-point failure skips ci and blocks the merge, rather than being an early step buried in the ci log. Pipeline shape: build -> regen -> ci -> deploy. It needs [build] for the release bins (regen runs the built gunbc), carries the floor-gate toolchain prelude (regen_stage0 emits rustfmt-formatted .rs), and is read-only (no push — the generated-artifact heal is a separate job with its own contents:write grant)."

fn ci_regen_job() -> Job {
  Job {
    id: "regen",
    name: none,
    runner: gunbc_ci_selected_runner_spec(),
    steps: concat(ci_floor_job_prelude_steps(), [ci_release_bins_download_step(), ci_release_bins_unpack_verify_step(), ci_regen_floor_step()]),
    needs: ["build"],
    env: none,
    outputs: none,
    if_condition: none,
    timeout_minutes: Present { value: gunbc_ci_regen_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() },
    continue_on_error: none,
    concurrency: none,
    permissions: none
  }
}

data ci_merge_group_trigger_note: String = "merge_group trigger: the merge queue constructs the tree that will actually land on main and asks for checks on THAT tree — the queue is the operational realization of gunbc.merge_admission KeyedReceipt on the tree axis (the verdict's identity IS the landing tree's identity), and the roster axis rides along because the gate roster is in-tree, so a roster change is a tree change. The theorem that this is the policy admitting zero unverified tips across every bounded interleaving — and that GitHub's strict-up-to-date boolean is NOT sufficient — is test.claim.merge_lifecycle_interleaving_witness. Queue runs see github.ref = gh-readonly-queue/*, so the deploy job's main-push guard skips them, the concurrency group falls through pull_request.number to github.ref (shared per queue ref; cancel-in-progress is false for merge_group), and the merge-admission stamp takes its non-PR arm (absent pr_number). If the floor's merge-base diff observation cannot resolve on a queue ref it falls through to the full floor — fail-closed, never widening; affected-set-scoping queue runs is a later optimization. The trigger is inert until the operator adds the merge_queue rule to the main ruleset (Rulesets API write needs the admin grant this integration lacks — gunbc.plans.branch_merge_admission_model section 5); land the trigger FIRST, flip the rule SECOND, else the queue waits forever on a check the workflow never reports."

data ci_workflow: Workflow = {
  name: "ci",
  on: [
    WorkflowDispatch {
      inputs: [
        DispatchInput {
          name: "expected_healed_sha",
          description: Present { value: "Immutable healed commit required by an auto-heal revalidation run" },
          required: false,
          default: none,
          type: InputString
        }
      ]
    },
    Push { branches: [gunbc_default_branch_name], paths: [] },
    PullRequest {
      branches: [gunbc_default_branch_name],
      types: [Opened, Synchronize, Reopened, ReadyForReview]
    },
    MergeGroup
  ],
  concurrency: Present {
    value: ConcurrencyMappingQueueNotMax {

      group: ci_concurrency_group(),
      cancel_in_progress: Present { value: CancelInProgressExpression { expression: ci_concurrency_cancel_in_progress_expression() } },
      explicit_single: none
    }
  },
  env: Present {
    value: [
      kv(key: "CARGO_TERM_COLOR", value: yaml_string(s: "always")),
      kv(key: "RUSTFLAGS", value: yaml_string(s: "-D warnings"))
    ]
  },
  permissions: Present {
    value: WorkflowPermissions {
      contents: Present { value: extdeps.github.actions.PermRead },
      pull_requests: Present { value: extdeps.github.actions.PermRead },
      issues: none,
      actions: none,
      id_token: none
    }
  },
  jobs: [ci_build_job(), ci_regen_job(), ci_job(), ci_heal_generated_artifacts_job(), ci_fleet_job()]
}
